# Cloudflare Pages headers. public/ is copied into dist/ at build time, so this
# lands at https://jva-music.com/_headers and Pages applies it at the edge.
#
# Why this file exists:
# The raw PDF files under /pdfs/ were being indexed as search results in their
# own right and were competing with their own landing pages. Measured in Search
# Console over 90 days: /pdfs/drumset/three-basic-rock-beats.pdf took 5 clicks
# at average position 11.7 while its landing page took 2 at 6.6, and
# /pdfs/transcriptions/island-in-the-sun.pdf was ranking at 4.8. Eight raw-file
# URLs carried 85 impressions and 11 clicks that all landed on a bare file:
# no schema, no thumbnail, no "Download PDF" CTA, no route into the rest of the
# site. The landing page should be the indexed URL for every one of them.
#
# noindex rather than a robots.txt Disallow, deliberately: Google has to be
# able to fetch the file to read this header. A Disallow would hide the PDF
# from the crawler and leave it indexed forever.
#
# Pattern note: keep these narrow. A previous wildcard _redirects rule broke
# every CSS/JS/image request on the site (see astro.config.mjs history and
# commit 86f9612). These two rules only ever match files ending in .pdf under
# /pdfs/.

/pdfs/*.pdf
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

/pdfs/*/*.pdf
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
